overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys are sequences of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":" symbols, stored as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"text":" holds words,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"text":" the same words scalar by scalar, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"text":" byte strings. Lookup,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O(","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}]},{"text":") for a key of ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"text":" symbols","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;"},{